<article class="env-lemma" id="00W6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00W6">Lemma <span data-tag="00W6">7.10.5</span>.</a> Given a pair of coverings $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ and $\{ V_ j \to U\} $ of a given object $U$ of the site $\mathcal{C}$, there exists a covering which is a common refinement. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $\mathcal{C}$ is a site we have that for every $i$ the family $\{ V_ j \times _ U U_ i \to U_ i\} _ j$ is a covering. And, then another axiom implies that $\{ V_ j \times _ U U_ i \to U\} _{i, j}$ is a covering of $U$. Clearly this covering refines both given coverings. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>